> Labeled duplicates and coordinate transformations

Equal coordinates do not merge input records. Distinct vertex indices
can be connected by a zero-length edge, and the algorithm still accepts
exactly n-1 edges for n>0. The next fixture adds a second record at the
unit square's origin. Its tree has one zero-length edge and three unit
edges. Plot markers at identical coordinates overlap; the table keeps
the separate vertex identities and their zero edge visible.

Translation cancels in pair differences. Multiplying every coordinate
by a positive factor a multiplies all exact distances and the minimum
length by a; the selected tree can be retained. These identities are
mathematical statements. In general floating rounding can alter very
close ties. Here the exact integer translation and factor three keep
all selected lengths exactly representable, and the stable selected
endpoint sequence is checked directly.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/euclidean_mst_duplicates.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");const std::vector<dm::algorithms::Point2D> p{{0,0},{0,0},{1,0},{1,1},{0,1}};auto q=p;
  for(auto& v:q){v.x=3*v.x+5;v.y=3*v.y-2;}
  const auto a=dm::algorithms::euclidean_minimum_spanning_tree_trace(p),b=dm::algorithms::euclidean_minimum_spanning_tree_trace(q);
  std::print("Labeled duplicates: vertices {}; accepted edges {}; original length {}; transformed length {}.\n\n",p.size(),a.kruskal.outcome.result.edges.size(),a.kruskal.outcome.result.total_weight,b.kruskal.outcome.result.total_weight);
  std::print("| accepted order | u | v | original length | transformed length |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<a.kruskal.outcome.result.edges.size();++i){auto [u,v,w]=a.kruskal.outcome.result.edges[i];auto [u2,v2,w2]=b.kruskal.outcome.result.edges.at(i);if(u!=u2||v!=v2||w2!=3*w)throw std::runtime_error("transformed tree identity failed");std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",i,u,v,w,w2);}
  dm::graphics::RLayout layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2);
  for(const auto* t:{&a,&b}){auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();std::vector<double> x,y;for(const auto& v:t->points){x.push_back(v.x);y.push_back(v.y);}for(auto [u,v,w]:t->kruskal.outcome.result.edges)plot.line({t->points[u].x,t->points[v].x},{t->points[u].y,t->points[v].y},"",{37,99,235});plot.points(x,y,"vertices",{220,38,38},6).title(t==&a?"Duplicate origin, original coordinates":"Scale three and translate (5,-2)").x_label("x coordinate").y_label("y coordinate");layout.add(plot);}
  layout.size(1100,520).title("Same labeled minimum tree; duplicate point markers overlap").fit_panels().save_svg("build/euclidean_mst_duplicates.svg");
}
```
