\alttext(Two plots show log-base-two pair and scan counts and retained trace records for seven line sizes, with exact known minimum lengths in the table.)

A generated geometric workload is appropriate for these exact properties;
an unrelated real dataset would not establish the cut proof or the
operation counts. The native tests additionally exercise random point
clouds, independently computed Prim minima, exhaustive small labeled
trees and a tree-path bottleneck certificate for every point pair.

> Finite domains, capture quotas and owned results

All coordinates must be finite, including singleton inputs that would
otherwise generate no distances. Pair arithmetic and container limits
are checked without allocating the requested graph. Finite coordinate
differences, hypot distances and accepted-edge totals are required;
numeric overflow throws instead of returning a connected tree whose
total is infinity or NaN. The generic Kruskal API accepts finite
negative weights, parallel edges and self-loops, and checks every
endpoint and weight before sorting. A disconnected generic graph
returns a minimum forest with is_connected=false.

The Euclidean trace counts C=N+M+S logical records: N points, M complete
input edges and S actual decisions. It checks known N+M before generating
or copying the graph, then checks each next decision online before
scanning it. The default quota is one million; zero disables only that
optional quota. Struct scalar fields, the separate output tree, runtime
sort/DSU storage, capacities and allocator bytes are excluded. This is
not a peak-RAM bound. Ordinary result/work calls retain no optional
history or quota. Every returned container owns its values, and errors
return no partial trace.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/euclidean_mst_limits.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");const std::vector<dm::algorithms::Point2D> p{{0,0},{1,0},{0,1}};const auto t=dm::algorithms::euclidean_minimum_spanning_tree_trace(p,8);
  bool short_cap=false,base_cap=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::euclidean_minimum_spanning_tree_trace(p,7);}catch(const std::length_error&){short_cap=true;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::euclidean_minimum_spanning_tree_trace(p,5);}catch(const std::length_error&){base_cap=true;}
  std::print("Triangle quota: points {}; input edges {}; actual steps {}; total {}; one-short rejected {}; base-short rejected {}; disabled-quota total {}.\n",t.points.size(),t.kruskal.input_edges.size(),t.kruskal.steps.size(),t.captured_entries,short_cap,base_cap,dm::algorithms::euclidean_minimum_spanning_tree_trace(p,0).captured_entries);
  std::print("Empty trace entries {}; singleton entries {}; checked pairs for 100000 points {}.\n",dm::algorithms::euclidean_minimum_spanning_tree_trace({},1).captured_entries,dm::algorithms::euclidean_minimum_spanning_tree_trace({{2,3}},1).captured_entries,dm::algorithms::euclidean_mst_pair_count(100000));
  const double nan=std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN(),inf=std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity(),max=std::numeric_limits<double>::max();int coordinates=0,weights=0,arithmetic=0;bool endpoint=false,geometry=false;
  for(double bad:{nan,inf,-inf}){try{(void)dm::algorithms::euclidean_minimum_spanning_tree({{bad,0}});}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++coordinates;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::kruskal(2,{{0,1,bad}});}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++weights;}}
  for(const auto& q:std::vector<std::vector<dm::algorithms::Point2D>>{{{-max,0},{max,0}},{{0,0},{max,max}},{{0,0},{.6*max,0},{0,.6*max}}})try{(void)dm::algorithms::euclidean_minimum_spanning_tree(q);}catch(const std::overflow_error&){++arithmetic;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::kruskal(2,{{0,2,1}});}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){endpoint=true;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::euclidean_mst_pair_count(std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max());}catch(const std::length_error&){geometry=true;}
  std::print("Rejections: nonfinite singleton coordinates {}/3; generic weights {}/3; difference/distance/total overflow {}/3; invalid endpoint {}; extreme pair geometry {}.\n",coordinates,weights,arithmetic,endpoint,geometry);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(65,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=3.5;box.height=1.5;box.font_size=22;
  d.node("points",{0,0},std::format("{} point records\noriginal vertices",t.points.size()),box).node("edges",{4.6,0},std::format("{} edge records\ncomplete input",t.kruskal.input_edges.size()),box).node("steps",{9.2,0},std::format("{} scan records\nactual decisions",t.kruskal.steps.size()),box)
   .edge("points","edges").edge("edges","steps").text({4.6,2},std::format("Logical capture C = {} + {} + {} = {}",t.points.size(),t.kruskal.input_edges.size(),t.kruskal.steps.size(),t.captured_entries),26)
   .text({4.6,-1.7},"Runtime, separate output and allocator bytes excluded",22).save_svg("build/euclidean_mst_limits.svg");
}
